# Dockerfile does `COPY . /src`, so without this the whole working tree enters the build context.
# A local .venv alone is ~175MB, and it lands in the COPY layer of every `docker compose up --build`.
# CI builds from a clean checkout, so this only ever bit local builds — which README and
# docs/development.md both tell you to run.
#
# `pip install "/src[web]"` needs pyproject.toml and media_sync_manager/ (including static/, via
# [tool.setuptools.package-data]). Nothing else. Checked: no setuptools_scm, so dropping .git is
# safe, and packages = ["media_sync_manager"] means tests/ was never packaged anyway.
#
# NOTE: these patterns are NOT .gitignore patterns. Docker matches each against the whole relative
# path with Go's filepath.Match, so a bare `__pycache__` matches ONLY a root-level one — nested
# copies need the explicit `**/` form. Hence the doubled entries below; they are not redundant.

# Virtual environments
.venv
venv

# VCS + CI metadata
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Python build / install artifacts
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
build
dist

# Test / tooling caches
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Not installed by the wheel
tests
docs
plans
scripts
*.md

# Local secrets / config — never bake these into an image
config.yaml
.env
